  "narrative": {
    "intro": "BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligated $666M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration won 126 awards so far, with an average award size of $5.3M, and obligations were down 24.1% year over year. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration draws most FY2026 spending from a handful of industry areas: Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $224M, Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounted for $164M, and Other Electronic Component Manufacturing accounted for $143M. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligations by fiscal year show a multi-year sequence: FY21 $700M, FY22 $689M, FY23 $644M, FY24 $1.1B, FY25 $878M, and FY26 $666M. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. The top NAICS categories concentrate most obligations, while smaller FY2026 markets include Aircraft Manufacturing at $54.1M and Engineering Services at $49.4M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has FY2026 to date compared with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligations in FY2026 are $666M. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligations trended from FY21 $700M to FY22 $689M to FY23 $644M to FY24 $1.1B to FY25 $878M and now to FY26 $666M. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligations are down 24.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries are driving FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing is the largest FY2026 market at $224M. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing follows at $164M, and Other Electronic Component Manufacturing follows at $143M. BAE Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration also records Aircraft Manufacturing at $54.1M and Engineering Services at $49.4M among other smaller categories."
      }
    ]
  },
